          <rect x="232" y="254" width="336" height="24" fill="var(--cream)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"></rect>
          <text x="400" y="271" text-anchor="middle"><tspan font-size="15" font-weight="700">100+ FT</tspan><tspan dx="10" font-size="13" opacity=".65">STRAIGHT APPROACH FOR TILT BED</tspan></text>
        </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="clr-plate-foot">
          <span class="clr-fig-foot-tag">SITE CHECK</span>
          <span>12 FT WIDE PATH MINIMUM</span>
          <span class="clr-fig-foot-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>GROUND MUST HOLD A 30,000 LB TRUCK</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>The rig and the room it needs, drawn with the figures our <a href="/delivery/">delivery guide</a> publishes. Tight access? A crane-set delivery solves most of it; the guide covers both.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  )}

  <!-- 04. THE ONE ASK. Three ask moments became one: the buy box button is an anchor to this block
       and the old closing cta-section is gone. A page that asks three times reads as a page that is
       worried you will not say yes. CallbackForm renders its own "Get Your {size} Price" h2. -->
  <section class="prod-action" id="talk-to-doug">
