      <p class="act-sub">No walk-up yard: a network of regional depots, an operating container company, and Doug. This is the part you can go and check yourself before you pay anybody in this business a dollar.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 05. IS THIS A REAL COMPANY. Evidence: across 379 competitor reviews in the Columbus corpus,
       scam language appears about 35 times and another 30 reviews describe relief that the seller
       turned out to be real; price is the complaint in 2 of 379.
       EVERY CLAIM IN THIS BAND IS ALREADY PUBLISHED ELSEWHERE ON THIS SITE. The proof cards are
       drawn from /container-buying-guide/, /about/, /contact/ and /delivery/, and nothing here
       promises anything fulfilment is not already committed to in public. Three cards from the
       mockup were deliberately NOT built, because they carried owner-confirm flags and one of them
       (pay by card, never wire or ACH) contradicts the accepted payment methods published in
       /terms/. See the handoff notes for that call. -->
  <section class="band band-ink" id="real-company">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head"><span class="band-no">05</span><span class="band-kicker">The first thing buyers want to know, answered in full</span></div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Is this a real company?</h2>
      <p class="band-lede">Most people buying a used container have never bought one before, and what they are actually afraid of is paying a stranger and never seeing a box. That is a fair thing to be afraid of in this business. So here is what you can check about us before you send anyone any money.</p>
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div class="proof">
          <span class="proof-tag">Who you buy from</span>
          <h3>A traceable business</h3>
          <p>Steel Box Direct is the authorized independent agent of Freedom Conex LLC, an operating company that sells containers. That is a company you can look up, not a phone number and a stock photo of a yard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <span class="proof-tag">Contact</span>
          <h3>A phone a person answers</h3>
          <p>Doug Froh handles every quote personally, start to finish. We answer calls 9am to 9pm Eastern, every day, and most quote requests come back within 4 business hours.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <span class="proof-tag">Delivery</span>
          <h3>A real delivery footprint</h3>
          <p>We deliver within roughly 250 miles of Cincinnati, across Ohio, Indiana, Kentucky and western West Virginia, from real regional depots. Beyond the home region we ship from depot hubs nationwide.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <span class="proof-tag">The number</span>
          <h3>A delivered total, not a sticker price</h3>
          <p>We quote all-in on purpose: the container, delivery to your ZIP, and placement on flat ground, in one number, so there is no freight line arriving after you have agreed a price.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="redflags">
        <h3>Red flags, whoever you end up buying from</h3>
        <p>This applies to any seller, anywhere, including us. If a seller does these things, slow down.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pressure to wire money, send Zelle or pay in cryptocurrency before you have verified who you are dealing with</li>
          <li>An invoice payable to a person's name rather than to a business</li>
          <li>Stock yard photos instead of photos of the specific unit, and no CSC plate to check</li>
          <li>A condition grade that is described on the phone and never written down</li>
          <li>Manufactured urgency: today only, another buyer is waiting</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="redflags-link"><a href="/container-buying-guide/">The full seven-point vetting checklist</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

